  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "### Local activity slots exhausted\n**Guide:** Failure modes: row 2  \u00b7  **Symptom:** Local activities pile up waiting for a slot.  \u00b7  **Cause:** Local activity slots sized from average latency, not Little's law at p99 and burst.  \u00b7  **Fix:** Re-derive slots from Little's law; set ScheduleToStart so starvation fails visibly (Java supports it for local activities).\n\n**What to watch:** Local activity slots available hits 0; end-to-end LA latency (schedule to completion) diverges from execution latency; with ScheduleToStart the overflow fails in 500 ms instead of waiting.\n\n| # | Variant | Phase | Length | What changes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | broken | 1 slot per worker, API 3.5x slower | 120 s | Little's law: ~8 calls/s/worker x ~165 ms = 1.3 concurrent > 1 slot. ScheduleToClose 30 s, no ScheduleToStart: the wait is hidden. |\n| 2 | baseline | recover | 45 s |  |\n| 3 | fixed | sized slots + ScheduleToStart 500 ms, API 3.5x slower | 120 s | Slots = API concurrency / max workers; ScheduleToClose 2 s; ScheduleToStart 500 ms. |\n\nRun it from the [control page](http://localhost:8088). Blue regions mark phases; red markers are crashes and restarts."
   },
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 7
   }
  },
